## 5.4 Comparison

| Complexity feature        |                      Video 1 |                       Video 2 |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------: | ----------------------------: |
| Average sentence length   |                   13.6 words |                    20.4 words |
| Longest sentence          |                     20 words |                      56 words |
| Relative clauses          |                      Several |          None clearly present |
| Coordination              |                     Frequent |                 Very frequent |
| Embedded clauses          |                      Present |                       Limited |
| Complex noun phrases      |                      Present |                       Present |
| Lexical diversity (TTR)   |                       ≈ 0.60 |                        ≈ 0.61 |
| Main source of complexity | Elaboration and modification | Coordination and accumulation |

**Overall conclusion:** Video 1 creates complexity mainly through **elaboration, modification, and relative/embedded clauses**, while Video 2 creates complexity mainly through **long coordinated sequences**.
Neither video depends strongly on difficult or highly sophisticated vocabulary. The principal difference is therefore **syntactic organization rather than lexical difficulty**.
